+**Why is Apple's Now Playing missing even with the bar expanded?**
+In Settings → Behavior → System extras, choose **Show while revealed**.
+**Always hidden** deliberately holds the assessment assertion even when no
+icons need hiding. The show option now remains available when a Pelmet
+replacement (for example the camera indicator) is enabled; that replacement
+must not force unrelated native controls off. To keep the bar revealed, use
+Settings → Displays → **Expanded**, with no items in Always Hidden.
+Native extras still disappear whenever an assertion is needed to conceal
+icons. This change does not provide a native Now Playing exemption during
+concealment. When native extras return, replacement items may also remain
+visible. Pelmet's camera/mic glyph stays available while hardware is active;
+click it to open Apple's own video-effects and microphone-mode panel. Available
+effects depend on the active app, hardware, and macOS (for example background
+replacement and Voice Isolation). Right-click still opens Privacy settings.
+
 **How does clicking the clock open Notification Center?**
 That's Pelmet working around macOS. While any icon is hidden, the system
 refuses the clock's click to open Notification Center (the same lockdown exam
